      "content": "It is important to be cautious, as combining home remedies for burns can sometimes lead to complications. While some people use things like honey, standard first aid suggests keeping the burn clean and covered with a sterile, non-stick dressing. If you choose to use an ointment, an approved antibiotic ointment applied *under* a loose, sterile bandage is generally safer than applying thick layers of differing substances. Please monitor it closely for signs of increased pain, spreading redness, or signs of infection, and consider contacting a nurse advice line if you are hesitant to visit a clinic.",
